prompt:
Implement Craig Reynolds' Boid flocking simulation using Three.js, displayed with flamingo models.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import through ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/Fox.glb;
(2) Clone 15 instances and randomly place them within the range from (-20,5,-20) to (20,15,20);
(3) Play the flying animation for each instance using AnimationMixer;

[Boid Rules]
(4) Separation: push away when the distance to a neighbor is < 3;
(5) Alignment: align with the average velocity direction of neighboring boids;
(6) Cohesion: move toward the center of the neighboring flock;
(7) Control the weight of each rule using sliders (id="sepWeight"/"alignWeight"/"cohWeight", range 0-2, default 1);

[Predator]
(8) A red sphere (radius=0.5) follows the mouse on the horizontal plane;
(9) A Boid accelerates away when it is within 5 units of the predator;

[Boundaries]
(10) When a Boid moves outside the boundary from (-30,0,-30) to (30,25,30), it turns back;

[HUD Display]
(11) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Flock center position (id="flockCenter")
  - Average speed (id="avgSpeed")
  - Separation/alignment/cohesion weight values

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - boidCount: number (15)
  - flockCenter: {x, y, z}
  - avgSpeed: number
  - separationWeight: number
  - alignmentWeight: number
  - cohesionWeight: number

Output a single standalone HTML file.
